It's time for the next set of assignment operators
that make a developer's life easier. Those described
earlier deal with addition and subtraction of one. 
Very often we need something other than addition or 
subtraction, or we want to use a value other than one. 
  
  
Consider the expression below:

i = i * 2;

It can be shortened to

i *= 2


This applies to every mathematical operator explained before.

